<div class="row" id="broken">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 class="doc-h2">What is broken</h2>
<p class="doc-body">The live menu is <code>layout.tt</code> → <code>pagetop.tt</code> → <code>Navigation/Menu.tt</code>. <code>Navigation/navigation.tt</code> is not on that path.</p>
<ul>
<li class="doc-body"><code>menu-theme.css</code> hides <code>.horizontal-menu</code> under 768px until the list has <code>nav-open</code>. The hamburger in <code>pagetop.tt</code> toggles that class.</li>
<li class="doc-body"><code>sub-menu.js</code> is loaded on every page from <code>js_load.tt</code>. On load it sets inline <code>display:flex</code> and <code>flex-direction:row</code> on every <code>.horizontal-menu</code>. Inline style beats the stylesheet, so the hamburger never wins.</li>
<li class="doc-body">Submenus fly out with <code>left: 100%</code>. <code>menu-position.js</code> is not loaded. Touch never opens <code>.submenu-item</code>.</li>
<li class="doc-body">A <code>.dropbtn</code> with a real href (Main → <code>/</code>) navigates instead of opening the panel.</li>
<li class="doc-body">768px misses tablet landscape and many phone-landscape widths.</li>
<li class="doc-body"><code>menu.js</code> looks for <code>#mobile-menu-toggle</code>. That node does not exist. Do not extend it.</li>
</ul>
<p><a class="doc-backtop" href="#toc">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="row" id="contract">
<div class="col-100">
<h2 class="doc-h2">Small-screen contract</h2>
<p class="doc-body">Layout is CSS. JavaScript toggles classes only: <code>nav-open</code> on <code>#main-menu-list</code>, <code>touch-open</code> on <code>.horizontal-dropdown</code> and <code>.submenu-item</code>. JavaScript must not set <code>element.style.display</code> on menu nodes.</p>
<p class="doc-body">The query, identical in <code>menu-theme.css</code> and <code>sub-menu.js</code>:</p>
<div class="doc-codebox"><pre>(max-width: 640px)</pre></div>
<ul>
<li class="doc-body">Under that query (a phone) the top menu is hidden until the hamburger is used. Submenus are accordions. Links wrap. Targets are at least 44px.</li>
<li class="doc-body">Above 640px the menu stays a wrapping row. A narrowed desktop or a tablet does not switch to the vertical list. Hover still opens dropdowns there.</li>
<li class="doc-body">No new CSS or JS file. No inline script added to a template that loads <code>js_load.tt</code>.</li>
<li class="doc-body">Colours come from tokens in <code>static/config/theme_definitions.json</code>. Do not edit the stale copy under <code>static/css/themes/theme_definitions.json</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p><a class="doc-backtop" href="#toc">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
</div>
</div>

